{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mqaswfamwxr","workspace":"/Users/imyu/Desktop/zonoid","title":"Lift per 1k tokens grounds lambda: bench smoke gives first utility label scale","summary":"Bench smoke results (2026-06-12, n=1 directional, 7 candidates) give the first empirical scale for the cost-aware gate label in [[note-mqaslontp50]]. lift/1kT = solve-rate lift per 1k retrieval tokens: task-transcript 14-18, legacy-id 11, locale-sum 8, flaky-dep 49 (smallest lift +50% but cheapest at 1k overhead), cron-next FREE (~0 overhead — injection made the run CHEAPER, agent explored less). interval-merge = 0 lift at 400-900 tokens cost — the canonical utility-label false positive that a binary solved-label would miss. Two design consequences: (1) cost_delta in the utility label can be NEGATIVE (a good inject prevents exploration and pays for itself) — the v2-v7 over-deliberation tax is not universal; (2) worthwhile injects empirically span ~8-49 lift/1kT, anchoring where lambda draws the worth-it line. The n=20 run yields per-candidate lift confidence intervals = 7 clean GOLD EVAL points for the learned gate (7 distinct note-task pairs, NOT 140 training examples — bench stays out of training per the oracle-contamination rule). Follow-up once n=20 confirms: fold these candidates into test/context-gate-regression.test.js ground truth and grade the current rule gate against them.","created_by":"main","valid_from":"2026-06-12T10:45:54.670Z","vec":[-0.0503365620970726,-0.005768254399299622,-0.020927803590893745,0.05382188782095909,-0.0737152248620987,-0.011613675393164158,0.061045415699481964,0.026995254680514336,0.02591594308614731,-0.02249223180115223,0.02280648797750473,-0.06915249675512314,-0.02668185532093048,-0.0409054197371006,0.06637883186340332,0.08060477674007416,0.0385589562356472,0.013896998949348927,-0.10247577726840973,-0.026660572737455368,-0.022589601576328278,-0.005232859402894974,0.028731506317853928,0.05896777659654617,-0.002259783912450075,-0.04934259504079819,